From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: allwinner: A733 combo-PHY -- register a Type-C mux so DP alt mode can be observed

COMB0 carries either SuperSpeed or DisplayPort and never both, and the lane
routing lives inside this PHY: there is no external mux and no select GPIO on
this board. The driver already registers the
Type-C *switch*, which is how TCPM tells it which way the plug went in. The
*mux* is the other half: it is what the DisplayPort alt-mode driver drives, and
without it nothing can ask for a DP pin assignment at all.

This registers it, and implements exactly the half that can be honest today.

What it does: accepts the state, records it, and names the pin assignment the
partner asked for.

What it deliberately does NOT do: touch the PMA. The vendor's DP configuration
fork -- the DP-side functions of combo0_configure_usb_dp() and the board arrays
lane_invert/lane_remap/typec_remap they consume -- has not been worked out
and ported yet. Writing a guessed DP lane setup into a PHY that
currently carries a proven 10 Gbps SuperSpeed link is exactly the trade this
tree does not make. That work is its own patch, against silicon.

Returning 0 rather than an error is also deliberate: an error aborts the
alt-mode entry, and then nothing is learned about what the sink offers. The
dev_warn() is the honest part -- it says the lanes stay in their USB
configuration and that there is therefore no video, so the state is readable in
the log instead of being discovered on a dark screen.

Matching follows the same rule as the switch, with a different property:
typec_mux_match() (drivers/usb/typec/mux.c) looks for "mode-switch" on the
remote port parent's fwnode, so the property belongs on the PHY node. The DT
side is patch `arm64-dts-a733-enable-dp-alt-mode-negotiation`.

Compile-tested against 6.18.36 with the full series applied.

Assisted-by: Claude

diff --git a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-combophy.c b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-combophy.c
--- a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-combophy.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-combophy.c
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/mutex.h>
 #include <linux/regulator/consumer.h>
+#include <linux/usb/typec_dp.h>
 #include <linux/usb/typec_mux.h>
 #include <linux/reset.h>
 
@@ -109,6 +110,13 @@
 	struct mutex		lock;
 	struct typec_switch_dev	*sw;
 	enum typec_orientation	orientation;
+	/* The mux is the DP-alt half of the same story: the switch says which
+	 * way the plug went in, the mux says what the lanes should carry. Only
+	 * the USB personality is implemented, so this records the requested
+	 * state and says out loud what it did not do.
+	 */
+	struct typec_mux_dev	*mux;
+	unsigned long		mux_mode;
 	bool			inited;
 };
 
@@ -739,6 +747,54 @@
 	typec_switch_unregister(data);
 }
 
+/* COMB0 carries either SuperSpeed or DP, never both, and the lane routing lives
+ * inside this PHY -- there is no external mux on this board. So the DisplayPort
+ * alt-mode driver reaches the lanes through here.
+ *
+ * What this implements is the *observation* half: it accepts the state, records
+ * it, and reports what the partner asked for. It deliberately does NOT touch the
+ * PMA, because the vendor's DP configuration fork has not been worked out
+ * and ported yet -- writing a guessed DP lane setup into a PHY that currently
+ * carries a working SuperSpeed link is exactly the trade this tree does not make.
+ *
+ * Returning 0 rather than an error is deliberate too: an error here aborts the
+ * alt-mode entry, and then nothing is learned about what the sink offers. The
+ * warning is the honest part -- the lanes stay in their USB configuration, so
+ * there is no video, and the log says so rather than leaving it to be discovered
+ * on a dark screen.
+ */
+static int a733_combophy_typec_mux_set(struct typec_mux_dev *mux,
+				       struct typec_mux_state *state)
+{
+	struct a733_combophy *cp = typec_mux_get_drvdata(mux);
+	unsigned long mode = state->mode;
+
+	mutex_lock(&cp->lock);
+	cp->mux_mode = mode;
+	mutex_unlock(&cp->lock);
+
+	if (mode == TYPEC_STATE_SAFE || mode == TYPEC_STATE_USB)
+		return 0;
+
+	if (state->alt && state->alt->svid == USB_TYPEC_DP_SID) {
+		/* TYPEC_DP_STATE_A..F are TYPEC_MODAL_STATE(0..5); the pin
+		 * assignment letter is the offset from TYPEC_STATE_MODAL.
+		 */
+		dev_warn(cp->dev,
+			 "DP alt mode entered, pin assignment %c requested: the PHY's DP personality is not implemented, lanes stay in USB configuration (no video)\n",
+			 (char)('A' + (mode - TYPEC_STATE_MODAL)));
+		return 0;
+	}
+
+	dev_warn(cp->dev, "unhandled Type-C mux state %lu requested\n", mode);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static void a733_combophy_mux_unregister(void *data)
+{
+	typec_mux_unregister(data);
+}
+
 static const struct phy_ops a733_combophy_ops = {
 	.init	= a733_combophy_init,
 	.exit	= a733_combophy_exit,
@@ -850,6 +906,30 @@
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
 	}
+
+	/* Same matching rule as the switch above, different property:
+	 * typec_mux_match() looks for "mode-switch" on the remote port parent's
+	 * fwnode (drivers/usb/typec/mux.c), so it belongs on this node.
+	 */
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_TYPEC) &&
+	    device_property_present(dev, "mode-switch")) {
+		struct typec_mux_desc mux_desc = {
+			.fwnode  = dev_fwnode(dev),
+			.set     = a733_combophy_typec_mux_set,
+			.drvdata = cp,
+		};
+
+		cp->mux = typec_mux_register(dev, &mux_desc);
+		if (IS_ERR(cp->mux)) {
+			a733_combophy_teardown(cp);
+			return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(cp->mux),
+					     "typec mux register\n");
+		}
+		ret = devm_add_action_or_reset(dev, a733_combophy_mux_unregister,
+					       cp->mux);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
